## Verdict
**The Game Over hold works as intended; nothing else changed; no console errors or failed requests.**

## The one change: Game Over hold
Test: start a run, then mash Enter (or Space, or click the button) every ~30 ms through the moment of death.
| Input while dying | Result |
|---|---|
| Enter mashed | Game Over screen stayed up; restart happened 0.56 s after death |
| Space mashed | stayed up; restart 0.58 s after death |
| Mouse click on button, repeated | stayed up; restart 0.54 s after death |
- At +0.2 s after death the screen was showing "Game Over / Final score / Play again" with the button greyed out (disabled, `02-gameover-held-*.png`), so the player can see the score and that the button is not yet live. (Measured times include my ~30 ms polling, so the hold is the specified ~0.5 s.)
- After waiting 700 ms: button enabled and focused; one Space press starts a **fresh** game (score 0, length 3, HUD 0, `04-fresh-play.png`).
- With a real score: bot run died at score 15; Game Over showed "Final score: 15 / New best score!"; next run started at score 0, length 3 (`run2.log`, `07-gameover-run1-wall.png`).
- Full cycle title → play → game over → play again done in each run above; wall death observed; self-collision unchanged from playtest-3 (not re-triggered in this round).
- Console errors / warnings / failed or 4xx requests across all runs: **none**. Sounds: `start.ogg`, `music.ogg`, `gameover.ogg` fire as before on each cycle.

